                        "source_entry_id": "5d6ae9c8-5c32-3b9b-956d-1037754da7e5",
                        "source_sense_id": "64194d52-b813-317b-8f82-a7c7b2561744",
                        "target_lang_word": "left",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "left",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "08bb0458-c9ae-3d6f-add0-e9ddad1f0758",
                                        "entry_id": "7650f8e1-59fb-32a4-b125-78bb68884edc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Designating the side of the body toward the west when one is facing north; the side of the body on which the heart is located in most humans; the opposite of right. This arrow points to the reader's left: ←"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1e720536-bbeb-44ec-b7d7-b599fe503ff9",
                                                "sense_id": "08bb0458-c9ae-3d6f-add0-e9ddad1f0758",
                                                "text": "Near-synonym: port"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5026852a-b2d2-4f28-8382-8905f9c34c3b",
                                                "sense_id": "08bb0458-c9ae-3d6f-add0-e9ddad1f0758",
                                                "text": "The left side."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dfe9075d-f7fa-320f-b223-4c2c93c52ddb",
                                        "entry_id": "7650f8e1-59fb-32a4-b125-78bb68884edc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Anticlockwise, particularly when describing a change in direction or orientation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "18667599-82e5-4c7d-83f9-123081f197bc",
                                                "sense_id": "dfe9075d-f7fa-320f-b223-4c2c93c52ddb",
                                                "text": "The road up ahead contains a left bend."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2327d0de-baad-4f90-afc4-34eee25c892e",
                                                "sense_id": "dfe9075d-f7fa-320f-b223-4c2c93c52ddb",
                                                "text": "Rotate the bolt to the left to loosen it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ee9004ad-2ea6-350e-9c4f-80bd46658fb5",
                                        "entry_id": "7650f8e1-59fb-32a4-b125-78bb68884edc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Designating the bank of a river (etc.) on one's left when facing downstream (i.e. facing forward while floating with the current); that is, the north bank of a river that flows eastward. If this arrow: ⥲ shows the direction of the current, the tilde is on the left side of the river."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c973c61-d658-41e6-ac9f-1a55f4d58568",
                                                "sense_id": "ee9004ad-2ea6-350e-9c4f-80bd46658fb5",
                                                "text": "The Eiffel Tower is on the left bank of the Seine."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b34c7c8-d7aa-412c-a477-958b5082f077",
                                                "sense_id": "ee9004ad-2ea6-350e-9c4f-80bd46658fb5",
                                                "text": "The following dispatch has been received from Viceroy Alexieff, dated Mukden, March 22:\n“Gen. Mitchenkow reports that on March 17 our scouts approached Anju and observed on the left bank of the Ching Chong river, opposite Anju, retrenchments made by the enemy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "43e92a46-99c6-3e8e-b674-28ccdda250d2",
                                        "entry_id": "7650f8e1-59fb-32a4-b125-78bb68884edc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Left-wing; pertaining to the political left."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c1de0b2e-a459-4dc8-af4b-598e4af1934b",
                                                "sense_id": "43e92a46-99c6-3e8e-b674-28ccdda250d2",
                                                "text": "It should be noted that there is now no intelligentsia that is not in some sense \"Left\". Perhaps the last right-wing intellectual was T. E. Lawrence. Since about 1930 everyone describable as an “intellectual” has lived in a state of chronic discontent with the existing order."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0058ebec-772b-41ea-b5b7-63353cfffb24",
                                                "sense_id": "43e92a46-99c6-3e8e-b674-28ccdda250d2",
                                                "text": "Who does not know the practical man who in his own field denounces socialism as \"pernicious rot\" but when he steps outside his subject spouts socialism like any left journalist."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "left",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f3b26b43-adec-3b91-88f1-4982932bfd9e",
                                        "entry_id": "241e9a73-836b-3acc-871a-0ca062fe3515",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "On the left side."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "07341f94-ea50-3f6f-a872-44dfbbd5a66c",
                                        "entry_id": "241e9a73-836b-3acc-871a-0ca062fe3515",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Towards the left side."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "387303fc-1072-411d-b590-6e17578cacc2",
                                                "sense_id": "07341f94-ea50-3f6f-a872-44dfbbd5a66c",
                                                "text": "Turn left at the corner. NO! Your other left."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5069cfa9-a83c-355b-8a11-c9e5dfbd0744",
                                        "entry_id": "241e9a73-836b-3acc-871a-0ca062fe3515",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Towards the political left."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ed03646f-7503-45a0-bb69-024456626b21",
                                                "sense_id": "5069cfa9-a83c-355b-8a11-c9e5dfbd0744",
                                                "text": "The East Coast of the US leans left in elections."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "left",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d8714db5-2f1e-3bcc-a54c-8caf0966780d",
                                        "entry_id": "e1beb4e7-c6de-3446-a27b-f877b789c497",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The left side or direction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "94c9db82-dc79-3cc8-9d35-a0a7ee75afb1",
                                        "entry_id": "e1beb4e7-c6de-3446-a27b-f877b789c497",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The left-wing political parties as a group; citizens holding left-wing views as a group."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e710901-f2b5-4be2-8267-fb9f3323ba0e",
                                                "sense_id": "94c9db82-dc79-3cc8-9d35-a0a7ee75afb1",
                                                "text": "The Left left workers behind, thinking they had a winning demographic coalition. It hasn't really worked out for them yet."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e335b7d9-2dcd-3054-b20f-2f88b7fafa26",
                                        "entry_id": "e1beb4e7-c6de-3446-a27b-f877b789c497",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The left hand or fist."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d052c836-7681-381c-8ce1-3a15bc2bd9b9",
                                        "entry_id": "e1beb4e7-c6de-3446-a27b-f877b789c497",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A punch delivered with the left fist."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5cd21e11-3b5f-4ae7-8ea1-5199fb6cfccc",
                                                "sense_id": "d052c836-7681-381c-8ce1-3a15bc2bd9b9",
                                                "text": "The world 'as got me snouted jist a treat; Crool Forchin's dirty left 'as smote me soul."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1c5c2c08-2e7c-341c-bfcc-5722adbd092b",
                                        "entry_id": "e1beb4e7-c6de-3446-a27b-f877b789c497",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A wave breaking from left to right (viewed from the shore)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "left",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f1a8b051-2108-3a4d-bc24-7c39b9fe924d",
                                        "entry_id": "af4a01ca-f7b6-304a-b196-620d0377a971",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "simple past and past participle of leave (“depart, separate from; (cause or allow to) remain”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of",
                                            "participle",
                                            "past"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "88163756-1067-4b30-baa0-7a589a07fa2c",
                                                "sense_id": "f1a8b051-2108-3a4d-bc24-7c39b9fe924d",
                                                "text": "There's not much food left."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8411aee4-e5c2-45ff-8c87-a5216b7abf62",
                                                "sense_id": "f1a8b051-2108-3a4d-bc24-7c39b9fe924d",
                                                "text": "Afore we got to the shanty Colonel Applegate stuck his head out of the door. His temper had been getting raggeder all the time, and the sousing he got when he fell overboard had just about ripped what was left of it to ravellings."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c7316e3e-24d4-45e0-8631-cdf65c735bc4",
                                                "sense_id": "f1a8b051-2108-3a4d-bc24-7c39b9fe924d",
                                                "text": "Shepard: What's wrong with your assistant?\nDr. Warren: Manuel has a brilliant mind, but he's always been a bit... unstable. Genius and madness are two sides of the same coin.\nDr. Manuel: Is it madness to see the future? To see the destruction rushing towards us? To understand there is no escape? No hope? No, I am not mad. I'm the only sane one left!\nDr. Warren: I gave him an extra dose of his meds after the attack."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "left",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2a095561-0936-3a42-a033-299fb96acf64",
                                        "entry_id": "4be0be25-8e5e-3958-ab23-d60475f78565",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "simple past and past participle of leave (“permit”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of",
                                            "participle",
                                            "past"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "88d84fb4-827c-492f-ae53-1ae0c05f7717",
                                                "sense_id": "2a095561-0936-3a42-a033-299fb96acf64",
                                                "text": "We were not left go to the beach after school except on a weekend."
                                            }
                                        ]
